<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Širvintos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-war">Polish–Lithuanian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Širvintos was fought on 17–21 November 1920 near the town of Širvintos, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a>, between Lithuanian forces and the Polish troops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucjan-zeligowski">Lucjan Żeligowski</a>, who had seized Vilnius in October. Together with the simultaneous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-giedraiciai">Battle of Giedraičiai</a>, it halted the Polish advance into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> proper. A ceasefire followed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> supervision, but Vilnius remained in Polish hands.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Lithuanian forces halted their further advance at <b>Širvintos</b> and Giedraičiai in November 1920, but Vilnius remained Polish and was annexed in 1922.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania">Republic of Lithuania · Military</a></li></ul></section>
